      'parts.note.devkit': 'You need an ESP32 DevKit V1 board with 30 pins and a USB-C (Type-C) connector: the slot in the case is drawn for USB-C. Check the connector on the product page before ordering.',
      'parts.note.mic': 'You need the round INMP441 module, about 14 mm across: the seat in the case is made for it. Check the board shape on the product page before ordering.',
      'parts.note.amp': 'The case is made for a board of 18.7 × 17.7 mm, pin header up, terminal block at the opposite edge. Check the size and the pin layout against the product page before ordering.',
      'parts.note.speaker': 'The case is fitted to this speaker: square 78 mm flange, Ø60 mm magnet.',
      'parts.note.filament': 'You need two Ø1.5 mm filaments in this variant: warm white, 3 V, about 185 mm, 100 mA. The 47 Ω resistor from 5 V assumes a 3 V filament, so check the variant on the product page.',
      'parts.note.res47': 'Three pieces: one for each filament and one on the gate of the transistor.',
      'parts.note.res62k': 'Between the gate and the source of the transistor.',
      'parts.note.inserts': 'You need 11 M2.5 inserts (4 mm long, Ø3.5 mm): 3 in the body, 2 in the body posts, 4 in the top, 2 in the tray. They are melted in with an ordinary soldering-iron tip. The link is a kit of 220 pcs, M2 to M5; only the M2.5 ones are needed.',
      'parts.note.screws': 'You need 11 screws: 3 for the tray, 2 for the top, 4 for the speaker and 2 for the DevKit. The link is a kit of 500 pcs, M2 and M2.5; only the M2.5×8 ones are needed.',
      'parts.note.washers': 'Under the heads of the speaker screws.',
      'parts.note.wires': 'Several colours. The cores of a twisted-pair network cable work well. Lengths are in the table of the Soldering section.',
      'parts.note.charger': 'A cable that carries data, not only for charging. The USB-C plug body must be slim, at most about 10 × 6.2 mm, or it will not pass through the slot in the case.',
      'parts.note.petg_black': 'Body, top, tray, button cap. Part of a spool is used.',
      'parts.note.petg_white': 'The two ring arcs.',
      'parts.note.tpu': 'Feet, two gaskets, plugs.',
